From c319baca474375e7bf5c6ad8dbbf52d2a32595ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: des <denis.yesakov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 23:39:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] input: add LineDecorationProvider API for per-line
 decorations (P1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A new public trait LineDecorationProvider lets a consumer of Input in
CodeEditor mode attach a per-frame source of full-line tints + gutter
glyphs alongside the syntax highlighter and diagnostic underlines.

Surface:
- highlighter::LineDecorationProvider trait with one method,
  decorations_for(visible_rows, &App) -> Vec<LineDecorationItem>.
- highlighter::LineDecorationItem { line, glyph, line_tint, tooltip }.
- highlighter::LineDecorationGlyph with six fixed variants
  (DiffAdded/Removed/Changed/Conflict/Bookmark/Breakpoint) plus
  Custom { icon: IconName, color: Hsla } as the open hatch for any
  future glyph kind.
- InputMode::CodeEditor gains
  line_decoration_provider: Option<Arc<dyn LineDecorationProvider>>;
  defaults to None, no observable change unless attached.
- InputState gains pub fn set_line_decoration_provider(...) and
  line_decoration_provider() following the existing setter/getter
  conventions; setter calls cx.notify() so the next frame picks it up.

Render integration in input::element:
- A new layout_decoration_glyphs() runs in prepaint, queries the
  attached provider with the current visible-row range, and prepaints
  one Icon-based AnyElement per item that carries a glyph. Glyphs are
  positioned at the left edge of the gutter with a 12 px width — for
  line-number columns wider than ~3 digits the glyph overlaps the
  leftmost digit, mirroring the JetBrains convention. A follow-up
  micro-epic can extend layout to reserve a dedicated decoration
  strip if that proves insufficient.
- The paint pass adds a line-tint loop between the active-line tint
  and indent guides (so a tinted line still shows the active outline
  on top, and indent guides remain visible over the tint), and walks
  the prepainted glyph elements after the fold-icon paint.

Tests:
- input::state::tests::set_line_decoration_provider_round_trips
  exercises the new setter/getter end-to-end through an InputView,
  covering the default-None state, attach, and clear paths.

LineDecorationGlyph deliberately derives only Clone because IconName
upstream derives only Clone; LineDecorationItem follows suit. Equality
checks should pattern-match on variants.

Patch P1 of Sub-epic E (line decorations, fork-and-merge-back). P2
(editor_gutter_background theme key), P3 (gutter cursor style), and P4
(line hitbox accessors) ride on top in subsequent commits.
